# Scratch output from running a test by hand; the binaries themselves are in
# build*/.
#
# UNANCHORED, since the suite gained subdirectories on 2026-08-09. These were
# `/*.ppm` so they could not reach golden/, which is test DATA rather than
# output - but an anchored pattern also cannot reach unit/, corpus/ or js/,
# which is where a stray screenshot now lands. So: match at every depth, and
# then put golden/ back explicitly.
*.ppm
*.log
*.csv

# `!/golden/**`, NOT `!/golden/`. A pattern ending in a slash matches the
# DIRECTORY, and golden/ was never ignored - its FILES were, by `*.ppm` above.
# Re-including the directory would change nothing about them, and every new
# golden would still be silently unaddable, which is the exact failure the old
# anchoring existed to prevent.
!/golden/**
